              "replacement": "        // This situation should be rare (a superclass implements a method declared in an interface\n        // this class is inheriting).\n        // We allow for duplicate methods within the same class in the direct methods or the virtual\n        // methods, as we will register the first one and ignore the second one.\n        // Caveat: we do not allow duplicates across those lists, so this means that class A can have\n        // two `foo` direct OR virtual methods, but it cannot have one `foo` direct and one `foo`\n        // virtual.\n        size_t super_method_index \u003d\n            (hash \u003c mirror::Object::kVTableLength)\n                ? class_linker_-\u003eobject_virtual_method_hashes_[hash]\n                : dex::kDexNoIndex;\n        if (super_method_index !\u003d dex::kDexNoIndex) {\n          ArtMethod* super_method \u003d super_vtable_accessor.GetVTableEntry(super_method_index);\n          DCHECK_EQ(super_method-\u003eGetDeclaringClass(), interface_method-\u003eGetDeclaringClass());\n          DCHECK_EQ(super_method-\u003eGetInvokeType(), InvokeType::kVirtual);\n          DCHECK_EQ(interface_method-\u003eGetInvokeType(), InvokeType::kVirtual);\n          DCHECK_LT(super_method-\u003eGetMethodIndex(), interface_method-\u003eGetMethodIndex());\n          vtable_method \u003d super_method;\n"
